// Kelmscott: William Morris's Kelmscott Press (1891–98; the Chaucer, 1896; The Well at the World's End, 1896) —
// research/16-kelmscott.md. A black-ground style: the ornament is wood engraved, the black is the block's face and the
// white is what the graver cut out of it, so the vine and the letter are the paper left standing in the ink. Every form
// here is Morris's own, traced from public-domain scans (tools/tracecut.py) and printed again through the ink engine:
//   B T N P S     six-line white-vine initials (the Chaucer, leaves n313, n104, n213, n245, n313 of archive.org MorrisChaucer)
//   L sB sM sA sS sN sP sT   two-line initials (the Chaucer: a black letter edged in white, a white leaf in its counter)
//   hedera        the leaf paragraph mark (The Well at the World's End, 1896, the Met 354288, CC0)
//   sprig         the flower-and-leaves sprig that ends the red chapter heads (the Well)
//   knot          the interlace that fills the running heads to the measure (the Well)
//   band          the narrow border that frames the Chaucer's pictures (its frontispiece, Commons, PD)
// A printed style of the one library (kit/illum.js: rubricate(root, { style: 'kelmscott' }), as tests/kelmscott.html,
// which puts it in the registry in place of the breadth-first entry of kit/wayfinding.js). Its parts return
// { marks: [], letters: [{ shape, x, y, w, h, col, flip?, strip?, from? }] } (a traced block's box in page px; col 'k'
// black, 'r' red; a strip is a length of border, see strip()); print() rasterises each block (even-odd) into a coverage mask and pours it into the ink engine
// (kit/inkletter.js inkLetter), so the black's edge carries the ink's spread into the white as a press leaves it. Drawn
// (?draw), a block is engraved: its face inked, then the white cut into it along its stems (letterWriter
// walking the white's skeleton, in the paper's own colour), then the block's ink pressed once more over the cut.
//   initial(o) -> { letters, width }   paraph(x, base, u, seed, rich, n)   filler(x0, x1, yTop, yBase, kind, seed, rich)
//   breakMark(cx, y, measure, rank, seed, rich, u, n)   frames.{ quote, figure, code, pull, aside, nav }   palette.{ light, dark }
//   print(made, { dpr, kind, u, y, seed, animate }) -> { pours, letters, runs, y0 }   timeline(printed, kind, animate)

import { dist } from '../inkletter.js';

