// The blocks traced so far (research/16 lists each one's page): the six-line white-vine initials, and the two-line
// initials (a black letter, white-edged, with a white leaf in its counter, on a scalloped black ground). A drop takes a
// six-line block when it is deep enough to keep its white (over 6 x-heights), else the two-line one; a letter in the line
// the two-line one; either, the other if its own is not traced. (The float is as wide as the six-line block; a two-line
// block, a tenth wider, takes it from the gap to the words.) A letter with neither is set as a capital of the page's face
// in the rubric's red, as the Kelmscott books set a plain initial.
