// ---- palette -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Light: the Chaucer's ink (a dense warm black, its median 47 39 33 on the scan's aged paper) and Morris's vermilion
// (179 56 50 on the scan; brought back toward the colour before the paper yellowed). Dark: the block printed in the pale
// ink of the page's text, the cut being the dark page itself (the white-line block read as light on dark), the red lifted.
// w: the cut, the page's own paper (read from --paper), so a block being engraved shows the page through its white.
